Kernel: power_iteration_2d

Mode: idea

Outcome: failure

Idea: power_iteration_2d: One step of power iteration on a 2D mesh

Failure reason: command_failed

Design choices:
  - One step of power iteration on a 2D mesh
  - y = A @ x followed by x = y / ||y||. A is row-tiled along Y, x is
replicated. After local GEMV, reduce along the row axis to get y,
then a global reduce for ||y||. Host drives multi-step iteration.


Diagnosis:
============================================================
DEBUGGER DIAGNOSIS
============================================================
Diagnostic run:      Re-read pe.csl line 117 and the @export_symbol calls; check CSL docs: @export_symbol for pointer-typed exports expects the address-of the variable directly (e.g. &A_tile), not a @ptrcast expression, since the argument must be a comptime global symbol.
Diagnostic output:   Compiler error 'expected comptime-known function value' / 'expected global variable or function symbol' on the @ptrcast wrapper. The same pattern works for ptr_time_buf_u16 because it is itself a declared global pointer variable (line 39). The @ptrcast on &A_tile produces a non-symbol expression, which @export_symbol rejects.
Diagnosis:           @export_symbol requires a bare global symbol (variable or function), not a @ptrcast expression. Lines 117-119 wrap &A_tile/&x_tile/&y_tile in @ptrcast, which the compiler rejects.
Recommended patch:   REPLACE the three lines:
  @export_symbol(@ptrcast([*]f32, &A_tile), "A_tile");
  @export_symbol(@ptrcast([*]f32, &x_tile), "x_tile");
  @export_symbol(@ptrcast([*]f32, &y_tile), "y_tile");
WITH:
  @export_symbol(&A_tile, "A_tile");
  @export_symbol(&x_tile, "x_tile");
  @export_symbol(&y_tile, "y_tile");
Confidence:          high
Apply the recommended patch verbatim if it looks correct relative to the reviewer's rationale. If you disagree, address the underlying diagnosis another way — but do NOT ignore both this report and the reviewer.
